{"created": "2026-08-17T03:19:54.918825+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-17T03:21:50.732820+00:00", "id": 21972335, "conceptrecid": "21127270", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21972335", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21127270", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21972335", "metadata": {"title": "Collision Geometry of Joint Spectra", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21972335", "publication_date": "2026-08-17", "description": "<p>This paper studies collision geometry for a fixed finite joint-spectrum arrangement under a one-parameter family of affine scalar projections. It proves finiteness of the collision set, chamberwise constancy of branch order, and the spectral quotient theorem for exact commuting-Hermitian realizations.</p>\n<p>For the explicitly declared rational nine-point arrangement P9, the 36 unordered pairs split into 2 parallel, 10 interior, 15 endpoint, and 9 exterior pairs. The interior collision parameters on the unit interval are 2/7, 2/5, 1/2, 2/3, and 4/5, with 2/3 the unique interior parameter of maximal layer-count drop. An exact two-parameter rectangular family supplies an independent control with one interior collision at b/(a+b).</p>\n<p>Version 2.1 reclassifies the declared complex128 Rubik registration as a source-addressed Computational Certificate and makes exact promotion fail closed. The exact Rubik quotient corollary is available only under the conjunctive assumptions R1--R3: exact operator admissibility, exact labelled joint registration, and the exact averaging identity. A diagonal exact negative control proves that collision adjacency alone does not imply transport adjacency or nonzero projected composition. The Rubik triangle-versus-chain result remains a bounded Computational Observation.</p>\n<p>The numerical certificate records nine stable registered clusters and a maximum raw-to-P9 table discrepancy below 10^-15 under the declared implementation and tolerance policy. It does not prove exact commutation, exact rational joint eigenvalues, exact primitive idempotents, a moving arrangement, transport or composition from collision data, maximality, or information-flow preservation.</p>\n<p>Source repository:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/dooven-prime/rime-lite\">https://github.com/dooven-prime/rime-lite</a></p>\n<p>Paper IV of the <strong>Representation-Induced Mechanics and Evolution (RIME)&nbsp;</strong>program.</p>\n<p>Independent researcher; no institutional affiliation.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Chen, WuJun", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0007-9561-2892"}], "keywords": ["joint spectrum", "collision quotient", "Bose-Mesner algebra", "algebraic combinatorics", "affine branch arrangements", "finite-dimensional operator theory", "spectral projections", "hyperplane arrangements", "Rubik's Cube", "computational representation theory", "numerical spectral registration", "commuting Hermitian operators"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21571403", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/dooven-prime/rime-lite", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21581072", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21583070", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "dates": [{"type": "issued", "description": "Version 1 public release of Paper IV."}], "version": "2.1", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/dooven-prime/rime-lite"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21127270"}}]}}, "title": "Collision Geometry of Joint Spectra", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21972335", "self_htm